; Open-array rest-tail PRESERVE fidelity round-trip vectors. Under
; --preserve-encodings each captured tail element re-serializes byte-exactly via a POSITIONAL
; `{field}_elem_encodings` sidecar (a self-carried `any` element carries its own encoding); under
; --canonical-form a non-canonical-width tail element normalizes in position order. Capture-only
; (`@ignore` is rejected under --preserve-encodings). See tests/open-array-preserve-e2e/tests.rs.
cap = [uint, tstr, * uint]          ; typed tail — per-element encoding sidecar (`rest_elem_encodings`)
cap_any = [uint, * any]             ; any tail — self-carried encodings (no sidecar)
required = [uint, + uint]           ; one-or-more tail — per-element encoding sidecar
bounded = [uint, 2*3 uint]          ; finite checked tail — same positional sidecar
middle = [uint, * uint, tstr]        ; major-disjoint middle segment — same sidecar before suffix
exact_middle = [uint, 2*2 uint, uint] ; count-delimited same-major segment — positional sidecar
; Stream position (the cip36 skip-arm bug class): an open array is a member of an outer array; the
; tail loop must stop at the open array's end and leave the sibling for the outer decoder.
outer = [inner, uint]
inner = [uint, * uint]
